      "writtenOn": "2020-03-19T11:41:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if need to guard this block into CHIP_FAMILY_IT8XXX2.\n\nBecause:\n- CHIP_ILM_BASE is IT8XXX2 specific.\n- Currently, only IT8XXX2 uses RISC-V.  And use IT8XXX2 \u003d\u003d\u003d use CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL for now.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dddac35_fc344dd7",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T00:12:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there\u0027s something weird here.\n\nFW_OFF(x) is CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE + FW_OFF_(x)\n\nWhen you do ORIGIN \u003d FW_OFF(SECTION) - CHIP_ILM_BASE\n\nBut CHIP_ILM_BASE \u003d\u003d CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE.\n\nI don\u0027t know exactly how this should be solved, but I\u0027m not sure if we need something special for the IT8XXX2 part?",
      "parentUuid": "84e47cc5_b1162f54",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22a82fbe_401273bb",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T02:48:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel ILM is like a lot external storage on other chips.\nCould we use CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE instead? e.g. https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/core/cortex-m/ec.lds.S#55",
      "parentUuid": "2dddac35_fc344dd7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb6ef3f7_68c07488",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1153134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T07:38:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On IT8xxx2 chips, flash is mapped to ILM (base address is 0x80000000), and CPU fetches instructions from ILM. So we need to generate instructions from base address of ILM and then load them into flash (base address is 0) or FW image will be huge.\n\nWe don\u0027t need to add CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL condition here, because image works on both internal and external flash.",
      "parentUuid": "22a82fbe_401273bb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ee3b670_f21b776f",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275795
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-23T05:59:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IT8XXX2 and MT8192_SCP is the 2 use cases for now.  I will use\n\n#if defined(CHIP_FAMILY_IT8XXX2)\n\n#else\n\n#endif\n\nunless we have the third use case.",
      "parentUuid": "fb6ef3f7_68c07488",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d71fe9a9_c12cc8a2",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275795
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-19T11:41:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, to be generic, here should be only guarded by CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL.\n\nHowever, __flash_dma_start is only used by chip/it83xxx/flash.c.\n\nHave no idea whether need to keep both guards.  (and the same for the following similar situations...)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "f30374351af0b2d67cdfc5b88892eebbb1649496",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1d99686_5cb1e368",
        "filename": "core/riscv-rv32i/ec.lds.S",
